# Caddy in front of OpenBerry on a server: HTTPS with a free Let's Encrypt certificate, renewed by itself.
# Used by `docker compose --profile caddy up -d`. See the README, "Run it on a server".
#
# The address is OPENBERRY_BASE_URL from .env, for example https://leads.example.com. Caddy forwards every request to
# OpenBerry inside Docker and tells it the visitor's own address (X-Forwarded-For) and that the request came over
# HTTPS (X-Forwarded-Proto). OpenBerry believes these only from OPENBERRY_TRUSTED_PROXIES.

{$OPENBERRY_BASE_URL} {
	reverse_proxy openberry:8000
}
